# .gitattributes - line endings of the tree.
#
# The guard and the tests compare the reference programs (.ngc, .qprog and their
# summaries) byte for byte with the text the code builds, and the builder writes
# "\n". The references therefore keep LF in the working tree of every platform:
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows must not turn them into CRLF, otherwise a whole
# run of checks goes red for a reason of the checkout, not of the code.
* text=auto
*.ngc text eol=lf
*.qprog text eol=lf
*.summary.txt text eol=lf
